Worked Example - Using PathVariable for input
Step 1: Run the Application

Start your Spring Boot application
Once the app is running successfully, the API Tester page will open automatically in your browser
Step 2: Test “Get All Users” API

In the URL input field, type:
/api/users
Click the Send button

What happens:

The request is sent to the backend
The controller method without any input is triggered
All demo users are returned
Step 3: Test “Get User by ID” API

In the URL input field, type below URL one by one and Observe the response:
/api/users/0
/api/users/1
/api/users/2
Click the Send button

What happens:

The value 0/1/2 is taken directly from the URL
@PathVariable captures this value
The corresponding user is fetched and returned

